# {{title}}

A Zeyn Framework app. Zeyn is a Rust web framework: screens are rendered on the server, a small
runtime in the browser applies changes, and there is no JavaScript to write.

## Commands

- Run: `cargo run` then open the address printed in the terminal
- Test: `cargo test`
- Develop with `zeyn dev`: it runs the app and rebuilds and restarts it on every saved change; the open browser follows without a page reload. A failed build keeps the last good server running.
- Check the app without starting it: `zeyn check`. It also warns about a `#[screen]` or `#[action]` that no feature registers, and about a flat `screens.rs` or `actions.rs` that has grown past about 150 lines with several items in it. After a Zeyn upgrade, `zeyn check --fix` rewrites renamed APIs (deprecation warnings name them).
- Container: `docker build -t {{name}} .` then `docker run -p 3000:3000 {{name}}` (distroless, non root, `{{name}} health` is the health check). Configure with `APP_*` variables, such as `APP_SERVER__ADDR`.
- Sign in: debug builds use `DevAuth` (every request is a developer with full access); release builds, the container included, have no sign in until `src/app.rs` adds a real authenticator (`OidcAuth`, `JwtAuth`, `ForwardAuth` or `App::accounts`). Never move `DevAuth` out of `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]`: the framework refuses it in release builds.
- Standards are fixed by the project files: `rustfmt.toml`, `clippy.toml` and `[lints]` in `Cargo.toml`, `.editorconfig`, `deny.toml` (licenses and advisories), `rust-toolchain.toml`. CI runs all of them; do not loosen them to make a change pass.
- Show every route, screen, API and missing translation: `zeyn routes`
- New feature folder: `zeyn g feature <name>`
- New screen, one file: `zeyn g screen <feature> <name>`. It registers the screen in the feature and adds its title to every locale file (other languages get the English text to translate).

The `zeyn` MCP server (see `.mcp.json`) gives agents the same commands plus the framework reference.
`.claude/skills/zeyn/SKILL.md` is the Zeyn skill: where to read the docs, the rules, the language in
short, common mistakes and how to verify a change. Any agent can read it as plain Markdown.

## Structure

```
config/app.json          defaults; environment variables APP_* override them (APP_SERVER__ADDR -> server.addr)
locales/<lang>.json      every user facing text; all files must have the same keys
src/main.rs              loads configuration and starts the app
src/app.rs               the App: services, features, security settings
src/services/<name>.rs   services shared by several features, registered in src/app.rs
src/features/<name>/     one folder per feature
    mod.rs               module declarations and the Feature: route prefix, guards, screens, APIs, menu
    models/              #[entity] and #[model] types, one file each
    services/            services of the feature that read and write data (stores, clients)
    actions/             #[action] functions, one file each
    screens/             #[screen] functions, one file each
    components/          parts of screens (a toolbar, a panel), added by hand when needed
tests/                   tests that drive the app through its router
```

Each folder has a `mod.rs` that lists its files. `zeyn g feature` creates `models/`, `services/`,
`actions/` and `screens/` with a working starter: a model, an in memory data service, a search
action and a list screen. A feature that does not need a folder deletes it (the folder and its
`mod` line in the feature's `mod.rs`). `components/` is never generated: add it by hand, with one
function that returns a `Node` per file (`components/<name>.rs`), when a part of a screen is shared
or a screen file grows. `zeyn g screen` adds a file to `screens/` and recreates `screens/mod.rs`
when it was deleted. The layout is a default, not a rule: a small feature can keep a single `models.rs`,
`screens.rs` or `actions.rs` (the sample `notes` feature does), and `zeyn g screen` turns a flat
`screens.rs` into a folder the first time it adds a screen. A service that several features use
goes in `src/services/<name>.rs` and is registered once in `src/app.rs` with `.service(...)`.

## Rules

1. Every action and screen declares access: `permission = "feature.resource.verb"` or `public`.
2. The first argument of an action is its input; the first argument of a screen is its params
   (`#[params]` struct, or `_: ()`). Every other argument is injected: `Ctx` or a registered `Service`.
3. Saving takes `Valid<Model>`. Never validate by hand what a `#[rule]` can express. Rules across
   fields go in `#[model(validate = fn)]` / `#[entity(validate = fn)]`.
4. Every text a user sees comes from `locales/` through `t!("key")`. The compiler checks that every
   locale file has the key and that the arguments match.
5. Dates use `Date`, wall clock times `Time`, exact moments `DateTime` (UTC), and wall clock date
   times at a place `LocalDateTime`. Never store a calendar day as a moment. Use `ctx.now()` and
   `ctx.today()`; never the system clock.
6. Money uses `Money` (integer minor units). Never `f64` for money.
7. Lists take a `DataQuery` and return `Page<Model>`. Never return unbounded lists.
8. A new screen is registered in its feature's `mod.rs`; a new feature in `src/app.rs`.
9. Do not write HTML, CSS or JavaScript. If a component is missing, write a `Component`.
10. Keep secrets in configuration (`config.secret("key")`), never in code or logs.
11. Write code top to bottom. Once a chain of calls is longer than about 40 characters, put one call
   on each line, so a line holds one or two dots on average. `cargo fmt` does this with
   `chain_width = 40` in `rustfmt.toml`; do not raise it.
12. Keep files and functions small: one component, screen or group of related actions per
   file. A source file holds at most 300 non blank lines (`build.rs` stops the build otherwise) and a
   function at most 60 lines (clippy `too_many_lines`). When `screens.rs` or `actions.rs` grows,
   turn it into a folder (`screens/mod.rs` plus one file per screen) and move large parts of a
   screen, such as a toolbar, a form or a panel, into their own functions in their own files.
   The limits live in `Cargo.toml` (`[package.metadata.zeyn] max_file_lines`) and `clippy.toml`
   (`too-many-lines-threshold`); raise them only when the owner agrees.

## Before you finish

Run `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` and `zeyn check`. All must pass before you push.

## Framework index

Everything below comes from `use zeyn::prelude::*;`. The `zeyn` MCP server has the full reference
(`zeyn_docs` topics: `rules`, `language`, `protocol`).

### Macros (all are attributes)

| Macro | On | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `#[entity(table = "t")]` | struct | `#[entity(table = "orders")] pub struct Order { #[key] pub id: OrderId, ... }` creates `OrderId` and `Order::field` refs |
| `#[model]` | struct | data that is not a table row: filters, wizard steps, form input |
| `#[model(validate = f)]` | struct | `fn f(m: &M, errors: &mut ValidationErrors)` for rules across fields |
| `#[choice]` | enum | unit variants only; `#[label("...")]` per variant; becomes a select |
| `#[params]` | struct | screen params: `#[params] pub struct EditParams { pub id: Option<OrderId> }` |
| `#[action(permission = "a.b.c")]` | async fn | first arg is the input, the rest are injected (`Ctx` or a `Service`) |
| `#[action(..., audit)]` | async fn | also writes an audit record |
| `#[screen(route = "/x", permission = "a.b.c")]` | fn | returns `Screen` or `Result<Screen>`; no route means it opens as a window |
| `t!("key", name = value)` | expr | text from `locales/*.json`, checked at compile time |

Field attributes: `#[key]`, `#[version]` (i64 row version), `#[readonly]`, `#[label("...")]`,
`#[rule(required, min_len = 3, max_len = 50, email, min = 0, max = 100, unique)]`.

Field types: `String`, `i32`, `i64`, `bool`, `Money`, `Date`, `Time`, `DateTime`, `LocalDateTime`,
`#[choice]` enums, entity ids, `Option<T>` of any of them.

### Actions

```rust
#[action(permission = "sales.order.read")]
pub async fn search_orders(q: DataQuery, store: OrderStore) -> Result<Page<Order>> { Ok(q.apply(store.all()?)) }

#[action(permission = "sales.order.write", audit)]
pub async fn save_order(order: Valid<Order>, store: OrderStore) -> Result<Order> { store.save(order.into_inner()) }
```

Errors: `Error::NotFound`, `Error::Forbidden`, `Error::Conflict` (stale row version),
`Error::Denied(t!("..."))`, `Error::Validation(errors)`, `Error::Internal("detail for the log")`.
Field error from code: `errors.add(Order::code, t!("orders.code_taken"))`.

### Screens

```rust
#[screen(route = "/orders", permission = "sales.order.read")]
pub fn order_list() -> Screen {
    Screen::new(t!("orders.title"))
        .toolbar(|t| t.button(t!("orders.new")).icon(Icon::Plus).shortcut("Alt+N").opens(order_editor, EditParams { id: None }))
        .body(DataGrid::of(search_orders).mode(DataMode::Server).column(Order::code).width(120).filter().column(Order::total).sum()
            .on_open(|o| Window::open(order_editor, EditParams { id: Some(o.id) })))
}

#[screen(permission = "sales.order.write")]
pub fn order_editor(params: EditParams, store: OrderStore) -> Result<Screen> {
    let order = match params.id { Some(id) => store.get(id)?, None => Order::default() };
    Ok(Screen::window(t!("orders.order")).body(Form::of(order).row(|r| r.field(Order::code).field(Order::status))
        .field(Order::note).submit(t!("common.save"), save_order)
        .on_success(|_, ui| { ui.toast(t!("orders.saved")); ui.close_and_refresh(); })))
}
```

- Several `.body(...)` calls place several components on one screen.
- Quick versions: `DataGrid::auto(action)` (all columns), `Form::auto(model)` (all fields).
- DataGrid paging: `Paging::pages(25)` (default 50), `Paging::infinite(100)`, `Paging::virtual_scroll()` for very large lists, `Paging::none()`.
- DataGrid extras: `.row_style(|r| Some(RowStyle::Warning))`, `.flex(1)`, `.width(px)`.
- Screens without params: `fn x()` or `fn x(_: (), ctx: Ctx)` when something is injected.
- Page header: `.subtitle(t!(".."))` and `.primary(|t| t.button(..))` on `Screen`; key figures
  `Kpi::new(..)` or `Kpi::money(..)` in a `Row`.
- Destructive grid actions: `.row_action(..)` or `.bulk_action(..)` then `.confirm(t!(".."))`.

### Linked parts and lists

```rust
DataGrid::of(search_orders)
    .listens("orders")
Chips::filter(..)
    .drives("orders")
ui.refresh("orders")
```

- Parts that show the same data `.listens("topic")`; `ui.refresh("topic")` in `on_success`, a
  filter that `.drives("topic")` or `hub.notify` reloads them in place. No JavaScript, no reload.
- Dependent lookups: `Form::depends_on(Address::city, Address::country)`.
- Rows of another shape: `List::of(action).builder(|row| node)` with `.separator(node)`;
  `Repeat::of(items, |item| node)` for data in memory; virtual lists need `.row_height(px)`.
- File stores: `.files(RULES, FileAccess::read("x.read").write("x.write"), store)`.

### Components by area

Look here before you write a `Component`: each line names the main types and the call that
matters. The `zeyn_docs` topic `language` and the docs pages have the details.

- Layouts: `Row::new().col(node)`, `Stack::new().add(node)`, `Panel::new(t!(".."))`,
  `Card::new().title(..)`, `Tabs::new(..).tab(..)`, `Split::new(a, b).ratio(55)`, `ListDetail::new(label, list).detail(..).back(..)`, `AutoGrid`,
  `Dock` for panels the user moves.
- Data: `DataGrid::of(action)` for tables, `DataGrid::dynamic(action)` with `DynamicPage` and
  `DynamicColumn` when columns come with the rows; `List::of(action).builder(|row| node)`,
  `CardGrid::of(action)` and `Rail::of(action)` for rows of another shape (a virtual list with a
  builder needs `.row_height(px)`); `Repeat::of(items, |item| node)` for data already in memory;
  `Tree::of(action)`, `Chart::bar(..)`, `Kpi::new(..)`; `DocumentViewer::of(page_action, pages)`
  for paged SVG or HTML documents such as report previews (`.document(id)`, `.page_size(PageSize::pt(w, h))`,
  `.outline(..)`, `.search(action)`; pages are cleaned unless `.trusted()`).
- Forms and controls: `Form::of(model).field(..).row(..).submit(t!(".."), action)`;
  `.control(field, Control::Rating)` (also `Radio`, `Segmented`, `Listbox`, `Switch`, `Percent`,
  `Password`); `.depends_on(child, parent)` for dependent lookups; `.lines(M::lines, ..)` for line
  items; `Control::Code(CodeLang::Expression)` with `.complete(field, action)` and
  `.check(field, action)` for SQL and expressions, `CodeEditor::new(name, CodeLang::Sql)` outside a
  form; `RangeSlider::new(label, ["min", "max"], 0, 100)`, `QuantityStepper::of(action, target)`;
  filters `Chips::filter(..)`, `SearchBox::of(action)`.
- Colors and lengths: `.control(field, Control::Color { palette: BRAND })` on a `String`,
  `.control(field, Control::Length { units: &[LengthUnit::Mm] })` on a `Decimal` (stored in px).
- Runtime forms: `FormSchema::new().section(..).field(FieldSpec::text("name", label))` with
  `SchemaForm::new(schema, values)`; `PropertyInspector::island("designer")` edits what an island
  selects through `zeyn:inspect` and `zeyn:property`, checked as `FieldSpec::check` does.
- Linked parts: `.listens("topic")` on every part that shows the data; a filter that
  `.drives("topic")` or `ui.refresh("topic")` in `on_success` reloads them in place.
- Media: `Image::new(src).alt(..).size(w, h).lazy()` with `.placeholder(Placeholder::color(..))`,
  `.low(small)`, `.fallback(src)`, and `.priority()` on the first image only; a lightbox with
  `.full(large).caption(..)` or `.lightbox()`;
  `Video::new(source, title).file(..)`, `Audio::new(..)`, `ProductGallery::new(name).image(..)`.
- Commerce: `Price::new(money).was(old)`, `VariantPicker::new().group(VariantGroup::swatches(..))`,
  `FacetPanel::of(screen, &p).facet(Facet::new(..))`, `ReviewSummary::new().count(5, n)`,
  `Countdown::until(moment)`.
- Admin: `DiffView::of(&before, &after)`, `CodeView::new(CodeLang::Sql, text)`,
  `JsonView::of(&value, &ctx)`, `Barcode::code128(..)`, `QrCode::new(url)`, `Inbox::of(action)` with
  `NotificationCenter::of(count, inbox, ())`, `Kanban::of(flow(), search, move_task)`,
  `Calendar::of(search).at(p)`.
- Chat: `MessageThread::of(history).conversation(id)` (`.reply(action)` streams AI replies),
  `Composer::of(send).conversation(id)`, `TypingIndicator::new("chat").conversation(id)` (needs
  `App::socket`); the actions check that the user is in the conversation.
- Social: `Feed::of(search_posts).post(|p| Post::new(author, at).text(..).media(image))` with
  `.reactions(react)` and `.topic("posts")`; stories `StoryRow::new().add(StoryRing::new(name,
  StoryState::Unseen).image(src))`, the state from what the server stored about the viewer.
- Display and content: `Alert::new(Tone::Warning, ..)`, `Badge::new(..)`, `Progress::new(..)`,
  `DescriptionList::of(&model)`, `Timeline`, `EmptyState`, `Breadcrumb`, `Markdown::new(..)`,
  `Heading`, `Paragraph`, `Avatar`, `Hero::new(..)`, `Reactions::of(action, target)`,
  `Share::page()`, `RelativeTime::new(at)`.
- Shells: screens open in the app shell (menu, palette; `App::header(|h| h.search().account())`
  adds a top bar); public pages use `.shell(Shell::site())` on the feature, sign in pages
  `.shell(Shell::auth())` (`.split()` adds a brand panel); `MenuBar`, `StatusBar`.
- Actions and buttons: `ActionButton::new(t!(".."), action, input).confirm(t!(".."))`, with
  `.tone(Tone::Brand)` for the main action of a panel; `LinkButton::new(t!(".."), screen, params)`;
  grid `.row_action(..)` and `.bulk_action(..)` then `.confirm(..)` and `.tone(Tone::Danger)`;
  workflow moves `Transitions::of(..)`.
- Files: `.files(RULES, FileAccess::read("x.file.read").write("x.file.write"), store)` on the
  feature, with `DiskStore` or `MemoryStore`.

### Features and the app

```rust
pub fn feature() -> Feature {
    Feature::new("sales").route_prefix("/sales").guard(SignedIn)
        .screen(order_list).screen(order_editor)
        .api(search_orders)
        .menu(|m| m.group(t!("menu.sales"), Icon::Cart).item(t!("orders.title"), order_list))
}
```

In `src/app.rs`: `.service(OrderStore::default())`, `.feature(features::sales::feature())`.
Other app settings: `.auth(...)`, `.time_policy(...)`, `.rate_limit(...)`, `.api_docs(...)`,
`.theme(Theme::new().brand("#0f6674"))`, `.base_path("/app")`, `.tenancy(...)`, `.license(...)`.

### Services and context

```rust
#[derive(Clone, Default)]
pub struct OrderStore(Arc<RwLock<Vec<Order>>>);
impl Service for OrderStore {}
```

`Ctx` gives `ctx.identity()`, `ctx.now()`, `ctx.today()`, `ctx.time_zone()`, `ctx.locale()`,
`ctx.config()`, `ctx.tenant()`, `ctx.license()`, `ctx.t(&text)`.

### Recipes

- New feature: `zeyn g feature <name>`. It registers the feature and its service in `src/app.rs` (or prints the two lines when `src/app.rs` has no `.feature(features::...)` line); then translate its texts in every `locales/*.json`. Delete the folders it does not need.
- New screen: `zeyn g screen <feature> <name>` writes `screens/<name>.rs`, registers it and adds its title to every `locales/*.json`; translate the copies in languages other than English.
- New field: add it to the struct with rules, add `Model.field` labels to every locale, add `.field(...)` to the form and `.column(...)` to the list.
- New permission: name it `feature.resource.verb` in the macro; grant it in the authenticator or identity provider.
- Publish an action as JSON API: `.api(action)` on the feature; calls need an `Authorization` header.
- Long lists: never return all rows; take `DataQuery`, return `Page<M>`.
